        company: 'Epigral',
        inShort: ["**A Meghmani-group chlor-alkali maker at Dahej, Gujarat** that splits salt into caustic soda and chlorine, then turns three-quarters of the chlorine into higher-value products: epichlorohydrin (ECH, India's only plant), CPVC pipe resin, chloromethanes and hydrogen peroxide.", "**Good:** margins of 22–28% through a bad FY26, its own 132 MW power plant, and a doubling of ECH and CPVC plus a new epoxy plant, mostly paid from its own cash. **Watch:** the doubling is a quarter late, Q1 volume grew only 5% against a 10–12% guide, Indian CPVC plants ran at only 50–55% in Q1, and part of Q1's 25% margin was war-level caustic prices.", "**Verdict: own.** The group's best self-funded growth, and the price asks for no more than the ~12% a year I expect."],
