        salesDrivers: ["**The import price**: Chinese soda ash sells for export at $160–180 a tonne and landed imports cost about $180–190; imports fell to 45–46,000 tonnes a month in Q4 FY26 and rebounded to 73–74,000 in Q1 FY27.", "**Trade protection**: only a 7.5% customs duty applies; a new request to cap imports (a safeguard limit) is under investigation, and would be the biggest single help.", "**Solar-glass demand**, which could take about 8% of Indian soda-ash demand once new plants start in January–March 2027.", "**Bromine and vacuum salt**: ₹150–170cr of revenue at 40–45% margins from FY28, although meaningful revenue has slipped to Q4 FY27.", "**Volume is capped** at today's plant (near 100% use), so growth beyond that needs the Kutch greenfield: Phase I of 5.5 lakh tonnes at about ₹4,000cr, first approved in FY2017, with no date, no financial closure and its clearances challenged at the National Green Tribunal."],
        inputs: "**Salt (brine), limestone and coke** are the raw materials; **lignite and coal** make the steam and power the process needs. Limestone is partly imported from the Middle East, and thermal coal rose from about $120 to $136 a tonne after the war began. It holds four to five months of raw materials. Materials were 36% of sales in FY26; power, fuel and plant costs 25%.",
